[Music]  pretty richmond virginia there  virginia's governor signed a bill  yesterday forbidding local public school  districts from requiring students to  wear masks the law will go into effect  march first after republicans teamed up  with a handful of democrats to pass it  it lets parents decide whether or not to  have their children wear a mask in  school  parents in several virginia districts  have sued in opposition trying to force  the state to keep mass decisions in the  hands of local school boards  governor glenn younkin joins us now  governor good morning thank you for  being here i saw the ceremony yesterday  it was clearly a big deal moment for you  there in virginia i'm hoping you could  start by just walking us through how you  came to this decision at this moment at  this time  well it was it was a big moment for  parents and kids in virginia yesterday  and i was just very honored to be  partnering with democrats and  republicans in our legislature in order  to sign that bill you know what this  bill and now into law reflects is the  fact that parents are best decision are  best positioned to make these decisions  for their kids  what we said yesterday is that if  parents want their children to wear a  mask then they should absolutely be able  to do so and if they think the best  thing for their child is not to wear a  mask then they should be able to make  that decision as well it was a big day  for parents a big day for kids  and a big day for virginia yesterday  now governor in theory parents already  have the power to make decisions for  their local schools through their school  boards  what was the issue that you saw with  that process  well the reality of course is that  school boards are elected over an  extended period of time  and what we've seen over and over  particularly in virginia over the last  couple years  is that school boards are out of touch a  bit with parents and and so what this  what this law now clearly reaffirms  is what already is in virginia law that  parents have a fundamental right to make  decisions with regards to their  children's upbringing their education  and their care  and this was an important this is an  important bill turning into law for us  to reaffirm those rights and so virginia  parents now can make these decisions yes  they can make a decision for their child  to wear a mask if that's in their  child's best best uh best health  decision or they can make a decision for  their child not to wear a mask you know  this is this is about putting power back  into the hands of the people and this is  also about getting back to normal and  we're on the path to get back to normal  in virginia and that's why today is a  very big day for virginians  yeah a lot of people agree with that  they want to get back to normal there is  a portion of the population looking at  the positivity rate there in virginia  it's a above 10 percent for covet tests  i'm curious you have power still in this  law to take action if needed are you  looking at any particular benchmarks and  conversation with public health  officials or experts in your state about  when you might take action to maybe  reinstate a mandate or require masks in  school  well i have i have a spectacular medical  advisory board that i've been working  with for a long time and i speak with  the leadership across virginia from our  hospital association  frequently and of course our own vdh  virginia department of health and what  we've seen of course is omicron fall off  materially is far less severe and we're  seeing a lot of the pressure in our  hospital system in fact be relieved this  is the moment also for us to to laud and  appreciate and thank the hospital  workers across virginia and across the  nation for all that they do in order to  keep everybody safe we're on the back  end of omicron and i'm excited about  that i think that we need to continue to  recognize that that this pandemic  and kobit 19 aren't going to go away but  it is absolutely far less severe and we  have a path to get back to normal and  that's that's the path we're going to be  on in virginia  yeah governor i you know would be a  pioneering move if you were to publish  benchmarks that you were using to make  your decision so i am curious in our  final question here if if you would do  that and then the second quick question  is do you encourage parents to get their  kids vaccinated  well i encourage everyone to get  vaccinated but i also want people to  make that decision on their own  and again we won't mandate it but we in  fact launched a public service  announcement this past week in order to  strongly encourage people to get  vaccinated we know it's the best way to  protect yourself protect your family and  so we in fact had a great meeting this  past week in petersburg we had a great  meeting this past week in petersburg in  order to really work with uh the  people's community in order to get  people more governor we're gonna they're  gonna they're gonna take us to black  it's your first appearance on cbs  mornings it will not be your last we  appreciate you being here  i got to go to break though thank you  very much  governor glenn young thank you we'll be  right back have a great day

